      "body": "KDA eager and graph extend both receive raw beta, but the graph helper infers beta activation from gate rank. Kimi-K3 supplies a 4D gate, causing graph replay to skip the required beta sigmoid. Set `beta_is_raw=True` to match eager extend while retaining the existing gate-shape normalization.\n\nValidation: A semantically equivalent version of this fix passed GPU serving smoke tests with prefill/decode CUDA graphs enabled, including prefix-cache reuse; sampled activations and logits were finite. This one-line patch passed 16 isolated CPU adapter checks, including 3D/4D raw-beta inputs and padding; the unpatched helper fails the eight 4D cases. Python compilation, Black, and `git diff --check` passed. The existing CUDA graph/kernel test suite was not rerun for this commit.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38944173069](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38944173069)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38944173017](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38944173017)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38944173024](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38944173024)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
